# Experiment folders on main

**Doc link:** <https://github.com/brando90/cert-judge/blob/main/.cursor/rules/experiment-folders-on-main.mdc>

**TLDR:** Prefer a numbered experiment folder on `main` over a separate git branch, so Cursor, Claude Code, and Gemini Antigravity (Agy) share one tree.

Read `AGENTS.md` section "Research workflow: experiment folders on `main`" before adding an experiment, editing the paper, or touching another agent's folder. `CLAUDE.md` and `GEMINI.md` state the same rule.

- Put each experiment in `experiments/NN_<setup_name>/`, register it in `experiments/archive/layout.json`, and add its row to `experiments/README.md`. Fetch and fast-forward `main` before editing. Commit straight to `main`.
- One writer per experiment folder. Read that folder's `README.md` and `CKPT_*.md` first. Put your own run in the next free number, and name the agent and the date in the folder README.
- A leftover branch's unique work lands on `main` as its own experiment folder, or as `paper_latex/interim_drafts/<date>_<name>/` when it is an interim paper draft. Leave live experiment paths and `paper_latex/ICLR_2027_submission/` in place when the branch would move or rewrite them. The 10-13-2026 framing draft is `paper_latex/interim_drafts/framing_10-13-2026/` and is not the paper's claims.
- Run deterministic checks before marking an experiment folder done or deleting a leftover branch: run `python3 py_src/cert_judge/experiment_layout.py --check`, verify parity of any branch-copied files against the branch tip without reintroducing retired roots or secrets, and run affected tests before pushing to `origin/main`; run model-reviewer quality assurance (QA) when requested under `~/agents-config` Hard Rule 3.
